Here’s a clean, efficient Python function to test primality:

```python
def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:
    """Return True if n is a prime number, else False."""
    if n <= 1:
        return False
    if n <= 3:
        return True          # 2 and 3 are prime
    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:
        return False         # eliminate multiples of 2 and 3

    i = 5
    while i * i <= n:
        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:
            return False
        i += 6               # check 6k ± 1
    return True
```

It runs in O(√n) time and handles edge cases (negative numbers, 0, 1) correctly. Feel free to drop it into your script!
